;; The negative controls of repr/haskell's round trip (GTS81 (a); doc/haskell/FRONTEND-SURVEY.md, "As built: the crop's independence",
;; 2026-11-07), read with the Clojure reader by arbace.repr.haskell's compare-forms (:tree, the tree level: the subject's printed
;; module read again natively, judged against the reference module's original forms) and compare-text --bytes-only (:text, the text
;; level: the subject's print against the reference's original text, byte for byte) and compare-iface (:iface, the interface
;; level, the oracle tier's: the subject's printed module's interface against the reference's original). Each pair must differ, else the level fails:
;; a judge that calls these equal tells nothing apart. Pairs whose modules the run does not hold (--only) are skipped; beside them
;; each run checks every judged module against the next one (the first five pairs), so a run of two modules or more always judges
;; one. Keys are PKG/corpus-file, as the known files'.
{:tree [["array/Data/Array.hs" "array/Data/Array/IArray.hs"]
        ["deepseq/Control/DeepSeq.hs" "array/Data/Array.hs"]
        ;; a near pair: the same package, a module and its sibling of a few lines' difference
        ["containers/src/Data/Map.hs" "containers/src/Data/Set.hs"]]
 :text [["array/Data/Array.hs" "array/Data/Array/IArray.hs"]
        ["containers/src/Data/Map.hs" "containers/src/Data/Set.hs"]]
 :iface [["array/Data/Array.hs" "array/Data/Array/IArray.hs"]
         ["containers/src/Data/Map.hs" "containers/src/Data/Set.hs"]]}
